body: "## Hosted acceptance failure, not a demonstrated data defect\n\nCurrent main `aa53d5f0e83f2df158d22aa5687b59e3493444fd` fails the [Node 22 job](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-web/actions/runs/40926606362/job/123633690461): **883 tests, 882 passed, 1 failed**. Rechecked October 29 at 19:06 UTC: this remains the main revision, Node22 is failed and Node26 is still running. No claim of deployment or publication.\n\nThe failure is [test/idempotency.test.ts:587–610](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-web/blob/aa53d5f0e83f2df158d22aa5687b59e3493444fd/test/idempotency.test.ts#L587-L610), “PostgreSQL can serve each real idempotency sweep query with its partial age index”. At line602 it expects `idx_pm_idempotency_settled_at`, but the hosted plan is:\n\n```\nDelete on pm_idempotency_keys (cost=0.12..8.15 rows=0 width=0)\n  -> Index Scan using idx_pm_idempotency_created_at ...\n       Filter: ((status_code IS NOT NULL) AND (updated_at < ...))\n```\n\nThis also does not demonstrate the age cutoff as an index condition. It does **not** establish wrong deletion semantics, data loss, or a production performance regression.\n\n## Static context and source goal\n\nThe test extracts actual pending/settled sweep SQL, opens a transaction, disables sequential scans and asserts a specific index name and age Index Cond. It does not establish its own representative row distribution or ANALYZE statistics before EXPLAIN. Dependence on the existing test-table state/planner costs is a possible explanation, not an independently reproduced cause.\n\nBoth the legacy partial `created_at` index and the intended partial `updated_at` index exist in [schema.sql](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-web/blob/aa53d5f0e83f2df158d22aa5687b59e3493444fd/sql/schema.sql). The [real settled sweep](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-web/blob/aa53d5f0e83f2df158d22aa5687b59e3493444fd/src/idempotency.ts) filters on `updated_at`. A missing index is not demonstrated.\n\nCanonical [pm-web-ccie](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-web/blob/aa53d5f0e83f2df158d22aa5687b59e3493444fd/.agents/pm/issues/pm-web-ccie.toon), particularly the October4 review-round4 receipts, requires meaningful real-query partial age-index proof and negative controls. Current CI does not satisfy that acceptance.\n\n## Reproduction and acceptance\n\n1. Inspect the linked immutable hosted log, or run the unchanged PostgreSQL-backed test/full Node22 suite in a disposable environment.\n2. Determine whether table population/statistics, equivalent planner alternatives, retained legacy indexes, or SQL/index design causes this plan. Preserve the observed plan and database version/settings.\n3. Make the acceptance fixture establish representative controlled rows/statistics and test the actual production predicates. Separate index capability/eligibility from cost-based planner selection where appropriate.\n4. Keep a meaningful negative control that rejects missing/unusable age access paths; do not merely drop the assertion or accept any index scan. If alternate plans are admitted, justify their equivalent bounded work with query-plan/cost evidence.\n5. Preserve retention/outcome semantics and schema parity. Run the focused case and full current-head Node22/26 gates with exact counts.\n\nScope: hosted failure plus static inspection; no local database, provider or concurrency reproduction. Three all-status issue/PR pages and the relevant canonical record were checked before filing. Existing #275 concerns unrelated history-version/lifecycle assertions and is not this failure.\n\n---\n\n### GitHub comments (1)\n\n> **@unbraind** (2026-11-02T09:27:07Z)\n>\n> Closing as not reproduced: main has been green in every later run. Reopen if it recurs. Evidence: Failure at main aa53d5f (run 40926606362, 2026-10-29T17:59Z); no idempotency/schema source change since 10-23, and main Node 22 green in every later run: 40957638340, 41131955064, 41203058017 — planner-dependent acceptance; recommend closure as unreproduced, optionally with a stabilization note (Found in the 2026-11-02 triage of issues the blind issue watch missed.)"
